# F1 OpenViewer — environment variables (no secrets in repo)
# Copy to .env and fill in. Widevine path and version are practically required for DRM content.

# =========================
# Electron (Main)
# =========================
# DevTools in development
ELECTRON_OPEN_DEVTOOLS=false
# Relax CORS for development only (manifest/segment)
ELECTRON_RELAX_CORS=false

# =========================
# Widevine CDM (required for DRM content, e.g. 2026 replay)
# =========================
# The app can use Electron castLabs (Widevine included) or standard Electron with Chrome CDM.
# In both cases it is recommended to set path and version below to avoid error 6001.

# --- How to get ELECTRON_WIDEVINE_CDM_PATH (Windows) ---
#
# Folder that contains widevinecdm.dll.
#
# Option A – Chrome in Program Files:
#   1. Open File Explorer and go to: C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\
#   2. Enter the folder with numbers (e.g. 145.0.7632.162) = Chrome version
#   3. The path to use is: ...\Application\VER_CHROME\WidevineCdm\_platform_specific\win_x64
#   4. Check that widevinecdm.dll is inside
#
# Option B – Chrome in User Data (if WidevineCdm is not in Program Files):
#   1. In File Explorer address bar: %LOCALAPPDATA%\Google\Chrome\User Data\WidevineCdm
#   2. Enter the folder with numbers (e.g. 4.10.2934.0)
#   3. The path to use is: ...\WidevineCdm\VER_WV\_platform_specific\win_x64
#
ELECTRON_WIDEVINE_CDM_PATH=

# --- How to get ELECTRON_WIDEVINE_CDM_VERSION ---
#
# String like 4.10.2934.0.
#
#   1. In the WidevineCdm folder (the one above _platform_specific) there is manifest.json
#   2. Open manifest.json and look for the line "version": "4.10.2934.0"
#   3. The value in quotes is ELECTRON_WIDEVINE_CDM_VERSION
#
ELECTRON_WIDEVINE_CDM_VERSION=
